    "## Exercise 5: Universal Unit Converter\n",
    "**Objective:** Build a menu-driven unit converter with robust exception handling and clean function design.\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a program that converts between different unit systems. The user selects a category from a menu, then inputs a value to convert.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requirements:**\n",
    "- Support at least 3 categories: **Temperature** (°C ↔ °F ↔ K), **Distance** (km ↔ miles ↔ meters), and **Weight** (kg ↔ lbs ↔ grams).\n",
    "- Each category must be handled by its own dedicated function.\n",
    "- Use `try/except` to catch `ValueError` when the user enters non-numeric input.\n",
    "- Use a `while` loop so the user can perform multiple conversions before choosing to quit.\n",
    "- **Edge Case:** Reject physically impossible values (e.g., a temperature below absolute zero: -273.15°C)."
   ]
