    "---\n",
    "## Exercise 6: Password Strength Validator\n",
    "**Objective:** Practice string methods, conditional logic, and loop-based analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function that evaluates the strength of a password and returns a score from 0 to 5. The user can keep testing passwords until they type `quit`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scoring Rules (1 point each):**\n",
    "1. Length is at least 8 characters.\n",
    "2. Contains at least one uppercase letter.\n",
    "3. Contains at least one lowercase letter.\n",
    "4. Contains at least one digit.\n",
    "5. Contains at least one special character (`!@#$%^&*`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Output:**\n",
    "- 0–1: `Weak`\n",
    "- 2–3: `Medium`\n",
    "- 4–5: `Strong`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hint:** Use a `for` loop to iterate through each character of the password string and check its properties with `.isupper()`, `.isdigit()`, etc."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def check_password_strength(password):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Evaluate a password and return a score (0-5) and a label.\"\"\"\n",
    "    score = 0\n",
    "    special_chars = \"!@#$%^&*\"\n",
    "    password_length = len(password)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # TODO: Check length >= 8\n",
    "    if(password_length >= 8):\n",
    "        score += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    # TODO: Loop through characters to check for uppercase, lowercase, digit, special\n",
    "    # TODO: Use boolean flags (has_upper, has_lower, etc.) and add to score\n",
    "    has_upper = False\n",
    "    has_lower = False\n",
    "    has_digit = False\n",
    "    has_special = False\n",
    "\n",
    "    for char in password:\n",
    "        if char.isupper():\n",
    "            has_upper = True\n",
    "        elif char.islower():\n",
    "            has_lower = True\n",
    "        elif char.isdigit():\n",
    "            has_digit = True\n",
    "        elif char in special_chars:\n",
    "            has_special = True\n",
    "\n",
    "    if has_upper: score += 1\n",
    "    if has_lower: score += 1\n",
    "    if has_digit: score += 1\n",
    "    if has_special: score += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    if(score <= 1):\n",
    "        return f\"{score}  - Weak\"\n",
    "    if(2 <= score <= 3):\n",
    "        return f\"{score}  - Medium\"\n",
    "    if(4 <= score <= 5):\n",
    "        return f\"{score}  - Strong\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    # TODO: Return score and strength label\n",
    "    return score\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_password_checker():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Loop: ask user for passwords until they type 'quit'.\"\"\"\n",
    "    # TODO: while loop, get input, call check_password_strength, print result\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        password = input(\"Please insert password: \\n Insert 'quit' to exit!\")\n",
    "        if password == 'quit':\n",
    "            print(\"Goodbye!\")\n",
    "            break\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(check_password_strength(password))\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "run_password_checker()  # Uncomment to test"
