    "---\n",
    "## Exercise 7: Multi-Round Scoring Quiz (with Data Structures)\n",
    "**Objective:** Combine loops, conditionals, error handling, and dictionaries to build a stateful application.\n",
    "\n",
    "Upgrade Exercise 3 into a full multi-question quiz. The questions and answers are stored in a **list of dictionaries**. The program tracks the user's score across all questions and displays a final report card.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Requirements:**\n",
    "- Store at least 5 questions in a list of dicts: `[{\"question\": ..., \"answer\": ..., \"hint\": ...}, ...]`\n",
    "- The user gets **2 attempts per question**. After the first wrong answer, display the hint.\n",
    "- Clean all user input (`.strip().lower()`).\n",
    "- At the end, print a summary: total score, percentage, and a grade (A/B/C/F).\n",
    "- Use `try/except` if any question expects a numeric answer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "quiz_bank = [\n",
    "    {\"question\": \"What keyword creates a function in Python?\", \"answer\": \"def\", \"hint\": \"It's a 3-letter word.\"},\n",
    "    {\"question\": \"What data type is immutable: list or tuple?\", \"answer\": \"tuple\", \"hint\": \"It uses parentheses.\"},\n",
    "    {\"question\": \"What is 2 ** 10?\", \"answer\": \"1024\", \"hint\": \"It's a power of 2.\"},\n",
    "    {\"question\": \"What method removes whitespace from both ends of a string?\", \"answer\": \"strip\", \"hint\": \"Think .___().\"},\n",
    "    {\"question\": \"What built-in function returns the number of items in a list?\", \"answer\": \"len\", \"hint\": \"Short for length.\"},\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_full_quiz(questions):\n",
    "    score = 0\n",
    "    total = len(questions)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # TODO: Loop through each question dict\n",
    "    for quiz in quiz_bank:\n",
    "        attempt = 0\n",
    "        # TODO: Give the user 2 attempts; show hint after the first failure\n",
    "        while(attempt < 2):\n",
    "            # TODO: Clean user input before comparing\n",
    "            answer = input(quiz[\"question\"]).lower().strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "            # Using try and Except for digit based answer\n",
    "            if quiz[\"answer\"].isdigit():\n",
    "                try:\n",
    "                    int(answer) \n",
    "                except ValueError:\n",
    "                    print(\"Invalid input! You must enter a number.\")\n",
